 55 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 147 people. Revenue per employee of $7.6M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $444K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $206K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["MediaAlpha, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $871M market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +34% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $65M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.56\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 32% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 38% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3758224669988072},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $108.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MediaAlpha (NYSE:MAX) Stock: Insider Eugene Nonko Sells 9,524 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/mediaalpha-nysemax-stock-insider-eugene-nonko-sells-9524-shares.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794535747.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MediaAlpha (NYSE:MAX) Major Shareholder Mountains Insurance Grou White Sell